Here is the commit message:
AMBARI-19086. LDAP sync creates groups with Local type
 (Attila Doroszla via rlevas)

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the incorrect handling of group types in the LDAP synchronization process, where groups were being marked as local instead of LDAP. This was due to the use of a boolean flag (`setLdapGroup(true)`) instead of a more structured approach that utilizes the `GroupType` enumeration to define the group type explicitly. This inconsistency led to groups being created with the wrong type, affecting the LDAP synchronization functionality.

Here is the patch:

