private void setLdapGroup(Boolean ldapGroup) {
```
```java
public void setGroupType(GroupType groupType) {
```
```java
setLdapGroup(groupType == GroupType.LDAP);
```
Reason:
The fix involves changing the visibility of `setLdapGroup` to private, ensuring it is only used internally, and explicitly setting the LDAP group status based on the `GroupType` enumeration. This ensures that groups are correctly categorized as LDAP or local, resolving the issue with incorrect group type assignment during the LDAP synchronization process.


